abstract: "For odd m >= 5, q = 2^m, k >= 3 and a reduced quadratic APN permutation p of F_q whose derivative is nowhere zero and two-to-one, the least possible largest difference-table entry on unit differences over all lifts of p to GR(2^k, m) is q or 2q, decided by two invariants of p and the level; every lift attaining it is characterized, the coefficients modulo 8 decide optimality at every level, sparse representatives attain q after one coefficient digit is changed, and one added monomial gives optimal lifts of the explicit family P_{m,r}. Layerwise bounds for characteristics and two-round differentials follow. Lean 4 (v4.31.0-rc1, Mathlib d568c8c; 150 audited declarations, axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound; no sorry); the blueprint lists what is formalized and what remains on paper."
